Good question — worth clarifying before it causes a design mistake.

"Fixed, not user-customisable" refers to the set of status labels itself, not which task has which status. You (the person using the app) absolutely change a task's status all the time — that's the whole point of a status. What you can't do is add a fourth status like "Blocked" or rename "In-Progress" to "Doing" — the three options Todo / In-Progress / Complete are hardcoded into the app (which is why we put them in a SQL CHECK constraint rather than a separate editable table). Contrast this with something like Trello, where a user can create arbitrary custom columns — this app must not allow that.

